{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every field describes the whole burst, not its last notification. A burst is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one window as far as the merge is concerned, and “the last one wins” would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently drop every notification but one — on a debounce that exists"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precisely because bursts are expected, that is a change quietly going"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"missing rather than a visible failure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only notifications the observer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"accepted","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" are represented. A notification"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a store the observer was told it doesn’t own is dropped before it gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here; one whose store can’t be identified is always accepted, and sets"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifiedStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Why-there-is-no-history-token","text":"Why there is no history token","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The underlying notification carries "},{"code":"NSPersistentHistoryTokenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately not surfaced. That value is a CoreData "},{"code":"NSPersistentHistoryToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the watermark in "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"DefaultHistoryToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose only public initializer is ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — there is no supported","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion between the two, and SwiftData’s interface names no CoreData type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at all. Publishing a token that neither Swidux nor an app author can act on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be an invitation to misuse it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is lost by leaving it out: ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator.mergeChanges(into:policy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anchors its watermark on the highest token in the window it just scanned, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the token it needs is one it already holds.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stores one coalesced burst of remote-change notifications named."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"RemoteChange","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:18SwiduxCloudKitSync12RemoteChangeV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemoteChange"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/S